       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Four figures in ink at the extreme paper edge, no separators, read as 4.4.22. The same hand writes the roll number 2621 further along the roll (crop e3), which gives a control on the figures: its 1 is a plain rising diagonal, while both opening figures here carry the crossbar of a 4, and its 2 is the curl with a horizontal foot that matches the last two figures here. Called medium rather than high because the strokes are thick at this resolution and 1 and 4 share a descender in this hand; if the two opening figures were 1s the reading would be 1.1.22, so the year 1922 holds either way. The printed label on the leader (e4) reads 'WELTE-MIGNON. No. 2621 / Etude Ges dur, Op. 10, No. 5 (Schwarze Tasten) / Fr. Chopin / Gespielt von Tosta di Benici', agreeing with the written number. Crop e2 holds a single figure 9 standing alone, the rest of whatever it belonged to falling outside the crop."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
